/*!
@defgroup memcon MEMCON Driver
@details The MCUXpresso SDK provides APIs for MCUXpresso SDK devices' Memory Controller operation.

The Memory Controller (MEMCON) is the centralized memory power controller. It
accepts hardware power-sequence commands from PDCON when a power domain enters
or exits low-power mode, and also lets software directly update the memory power
state per slice. MEMCON is split into one global block plus twelve per-domain
slice blocks (S0 through S11), each owning up to twelve memory blocks.

The MEMCON driver supports:
  - Configuring global access control (16-bit domain ID, user-mode, non-secure
    mode, lock)
  - Enabling and disabling the MEMCON function clock gate
  - Configuring per-slice access control (4-bit domain ID + UM/NSM/LOCK)
  - Selecting the slice trigger mode: hardware only, software only, or both
  - Issuing a software trigger and waiting for the self-clearing SWTRG bit
  - Setting and reading the per-block low-power power mode (Active / Retention /
    Power-down) for each of the up to twelve memory blocks per slice
  - Setting and reading the per-block active power mode for each block
  - Bulk read / write of the MEM_SLPCFG0/1 and MEM_RUNCFG0/1 register pairs

*/
